# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file for the "Cite this repository"
# button, and Zenodo reads it when it archives a GitHub release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these rules in research or a benchmark, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "EyalSec Semgrep rules for Python"
abstract: >-
  Semgrep rules that find request data reaching a SQL query, a shell command,
  a deserializer, a file path or an outbound URL in Django, Flask and FastAPI
  code. Each rule has a test file, CWE and OWASP metadata, and a link to a page
  that explains the vulnerability class and its fix.
authors:
  - given-names: Eyal
    family-names: Gabay
    affiliation: EyalSec
    email: eyal@eyalsec.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/EyalSec/semgrep-rules"
url: "https://eyalsec.com"
keywords:
  - semgrep
  - static analysis
  - application security
  - python
  - django
  - flask
  - fastapi
  - sql injection
  - command injection
  - ssrf
